Here is a TypeScript function that removes duplicates from an array. The most common and idiomatic way to do this in modern JavaScript/TypeScript is by using a `Set`.

```typescript
/**
 * Removes duplicate elements from an array of any type.
 *
 * @param arr The input array which may contain duplicate elements.
 * @returns A new array containing only the unique elements from the input array.
 */
function removeDuplicates<T>(arr: T[]): T[] {
  // A Set only stores unique values. We convert the array to a Set,
  // which automatically filters out duplicates, and then convert it back to an array using the spread operator.
  const uniqueElements: T[] = [...new Set(arr)];
  return uniqueElements;
}

// --- Examples ---

